{
    "schemaVersion": 1,
    "description": "Input-only cases for the official Pandoc 3.11 extension oracle. No expected AST is stored here.",
    "cases": [
        {
            "id": "bracketed-spans",
            "from": "markdown_strict+bracketed_spans",
            "input": "[This is *some text*]{.class #key rank=\"1\"}\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "superscript-and-subscript",
            "from": "markdown_strict+superscript+subscript",
            "input": "H~2~O and 2^10^\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "inline-code-attributes",
            "from": "markdown_strict+inline_code_attributes",
            "input": "`printf()`{.c #call role=\"function\"}\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "header-attributes",
            "from": "markdown_strict+header_attributes",
            "input": "# Chapter {#sec:intro .unnumbered key=\"value\"}\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "gfm-auto-anchors",
            "from": "markdown_strict+auto_identifiers+gfm_auto_identifiers",
            "input": "## My Header\n\n## My Header\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "implicit-header-references",
            "from": "markdown_strict+auto_identifiers+gfm_auto_identifiers+implicit_header_references",
            "input": "# First Chapter\n\n[go there][First Chapter] and [First Chapter].\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "fenced-code-attributes",
            "from": "markdown_strict+backtick_code_blocks+fenced_code_attributes",
            "input": "```python {.numberLines startFrom=\"10\"}\nprint(\"hello\")\n```\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "link-and-image-attributes",
            "from": "markdown_strict+link_attributes",
            "input": "[text](https://example.com){target=\"_blank\"} ![image](foo.jpg){#hero .wide width=50%}\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "simple-table-with-caption",
            "from": "markdown_strict+simple_tables+table_captions",
            "input": "  Right     Left     Center     Default\n-------     ------ ----------   -------\n     12     12        12            12\n    123     123       123          123\n\nTable: Demonstration of simple table syntax.\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "multiline-table",
            "from": "markdown_strict+multiline_tables+table_captions",
            "input": "-------------------------------------------------------------\n Centered   Default           Right Left\n  Header    Aligned         Aligned Aligned\n----------- ------- --------------- -------------------------\n   First    row                12.0 Example of a row that\n                                    spans multiple lines.\n\n  Second    row                 5.0 Here's another one.\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTable: Here's the caption.\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "grid-table-block-cells",
            "from": "markdown_strict+grid_tables+table_captions",
            "input": ": Sample grid table.\n\n+---------------+---------------+--------------------+\n| Fruit         | Price         | Advantages         |\n+===============+===============+====================+\n| Bananas       | $1.34         | - built-in wrapper |\n|               |               | - bright color     |\n+---------------+---------------+--------------------+\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "grid-table-row-and-column-spans",
            "from": "markdown_strict+grid_tables",
            "input": "+---------------------+----------+\n| Property            | Earth    |\n+=============+=======+==========+\n|             | min   | -89.2 °C |\n| Temperature +-------+----------+\n| 1961-1990   | mean  | 14 °C    |\n|             +-------+----------+\n|             | max   | 56.7 °C  |\n+-------------+-------+----------+\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "fancy-list-and-startnum",
            "from": "markdown_strict+fancy_lists+startnum",
            "input": "9) Ninth\n10) Tenth\n11) Eleventh\n\n   i. subone\n  ii. subtwo\n iii. subthree\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "definition-list-loose-and-multiple-bodies",
            "from": "markdown_strict+definition_lists",
            "input": "Term with *inline markup*\n\n:   First definition.\n\n    Second paragraph.\n\n:   Second definition body.\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "definition-list-compact",
            "from": "markdown_strict+definition_lists",
            "input": "Term 1\n  ~ Definition 1\n\nTerm 2\n  ~ Definition 2a\n  ~ Definition 2b\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "example-lists-and-reference",
            "from": "markdown_strict+fancy_lists+example_lists",
            "input": "(@) First example.\n(@good) Second example.\n\nExplanation of examples.\n\n(@) Third example.\n\nAs (@good) illustrates, ...\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "fenced-divs-nested",
            "from": "markdown_strict+fenced_divs",
            "input": "::::: {#special .sidebar}\nHere is a paragraph.\n\n::: Warning\nThis is a warning.\n:::\n:::::\n"
        },
        {
            "id": "bibliography-citations",
            "from": "markdown_strict+citations",
            "input": "Blah [see @doe99, pp. 33-35 and *passim*; -@smith04, chap. 1]. @jones05 [p. 7] agrees.\n"
        }
    ]
}
